1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,743
Red text. Forty lines of it. And the build is broken.

2
00:00:04,293 --> 00:00:09,775
Most people panic here. They copy the whole error into a search box, and try random fixes.

3
00:00:10,325 --> 00:00:13,496
Today you learn to read a failed build in ten seconds.

4
00:00:13,496 --> 00:00:14,612
Four real failures,

5
00:00:14,612 --> 00:00:16,256
each with a different cause.

6
00:00:16,806 --> 00:00:18,918
A version that does not exist.

7
00:00:18,918 --> 00:00:20,044
An offline flag.

8
00:00:20,044 --> 00:00:21,100
A failing test.

9
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:24,550
And a four oh one from a real repository manager.

10
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:27,393
You will see every one of them happen,

11
00:00:27,393 --> 00:00:28,962
on the real Maven Central,

12
00:00:28,962 --> 00:00:30,169
and on a real Nexus.

13
00:00:30,169 --> 00:00:31,799
Then you fix them yourself.

14
00:00:32,349 --> 00:00:33,437
One honest note.

15
00:00:33,437 --> 00:00:35,954
Every failure in this lesson is real,

16
00:00:35,954 --> 00:00:38,267
and the lab you get does the same.

17
00:00:38,267 --> 00:00:40,172
I only planted the mistakes,

18
00:00:40,172 --> 00:00:41,260
a wrong version,

19
00:00:41,260 --> 00:00:41,736
a flag,

20
00:00:41,736 --> 00:00:42,144
a bug,

21
00:00:42,144 --> 00:00:43,165
and a wrong id.

22
00:00:44,715 --> 00:00:49,664
First, how to read a failed build. Maven prints a lot. Only a few lines matter.

23
00:00:50,214 --> 00:00:50,794
Step one.

24
00:00:50,794 --> 00:00:54,915
Skip everything until the first line that starts with E R R O R.

25
00:00:54,915 --> 00:00:57,233
The ones above it are just progress.

26
00:00:57,783 --> 00:00:58,400
Step two.

27
00:00:58,400 --> 00:01:00,250
Find the stage that failed.

28
00:01:00,250 --> 00:01:03,471
Maven works in order: resolve the dependencies,

29
00:01:03,471 --> 00:01:04,019
compile,

30
00:01:04,019 --> 00:01:04,979
run the tests,

31
00:01:04,979 --> 00:01:05,527
package.

32
00:01:06,077 --> 00:01:06,861
Step three.

33
00:01:06,861 --> 00:01:07,930
Read the cause,

34
00:01:07,930 --> 00:01:08,999
in plain words.

35
00:01:08,999 --> 00:01:10,068
Could not find.

36
00:01:10,068 --> 00:01:11,066
Cannot access,

37
00:01:11,066 --> 00:01:12,207
in offline mode.

38
00:01:12,207 --> 00:01:12,920
Tests run,

39
00:01:12,920 --> 00:01:13,561
failures.

40
00:01:13,561 --> 00:01:15,272
Status code four oh one.

41
00:01:15,822 --> 00:01:16,489
Step four.

42
00:01:16,489 --> 00:01:17,424
Fix the cause.

43
00:01:17,424 --> 00:01:18,359
Never hide it.

44
00:01:18,359 --> 00:01:19,962
No dash O to go offline,

45
00:01:19,962 --> 00:01:20,897
no skip tests,

46
00:01:20,897 --> 00:01:24,035
and never delete the dependency that complains.

47
00:01:24,585 --> 00:01:29,492
Hiding a failure is how a broken build reaches the server. We always fix the cause.

48
00:01:31,542 --> 00:01:35,446
Here are today's four failures, from the simplest to the most advanced.

49
00:01:35,996 --> 00:01:36,266
One.

50
00:01:36,266 --> 00:01:37,886
Could not find artifact.

51
00:01:37,886 --> 00:01:41,058
The pom asks for a version that does not exist.

52
00:01:41,058 --> 00:01:43,420
Maven Central answers four oh four.

53
00:01:43,970 --> 00:01:44,228
Two.

54
00:01:44,228 --> 00:01:46,677
Cannot access central in offline mode.

55
00:01:46,677 --> 00:01:49,965
A hidden dash O is stopping Maven from downloading.

56
00:01:50,515 --> 00:01:55,464
Three. Tests run, failures. The code compiles, but a test proves the code is wrong.

57
00:01:56,014 --> 00:01:56,390
Four.

58
00:01:56,390 --> 00:01:58,198
Status code four oh one.

59
00:01:58,198 --> 00:02:01,586
A real repository manager that needs a login,

60
00:02:01,586 --> 00:02:03,694
and Maven sent the wrong id.

61
00:02:04,244 --> 00:02:08,639
Every message points to its own cause. Learn the phrase, and you know where to look.

62
00:02:10,689 --> 00:02:16,620
Now the real thing. Go to the lab folder. Type: CD, slash opt, slash lab ninety-two.

63
00:02:17,170 --> 00:02:20,075
Lab ninety-two sets up four small projects,

64
00:02:20,075 --> 00:02:23,047
and a real Nexus on port eight oh eight one.

65
00:02:23,047 --> 00:02:25,682
The login password is in a locked file.

66
00:02:26,232 --> 00:02:27,720
Put the password in a variable.

67
00:02:27,720 --> 00:02:30,168
Type: export C O R P underscore PASS equals dollar,

68
00:02:30,168 --> 00:02:30,744
parenthesis,

69
00:02:30,744 --> 00:02:31,608
cat pass dot text.

70
00:02:32,158 --> 00:02:34,227
List the folder. Type: L S.

71
00:02:34,777 --> 00:02:39,961
Four projects. Not found, offline, tests, and login. We take them in this order.

72
00:02:40,511 --> 00:02:44,180
Failure one. Go into not found. Type: CD, not found.

73
00:02:44,730 --> 00:02:45,081
Build it,

74
00:02:45,081 --> 00:02:46,951
and keep only the line that says could not find.

75
00:02:46,951 --> 00:02:47,419
Type: M V N,

76
00:02:47,419 --> 00:02:47,692
dash B,

77
00:02:47,692 --> 00:02:48,003
package,

78
00:02:48,003 --> 00:02:48,549
and then grep.

79
00:02:50,399 --> 00:02:52,788
Maven is resolving the dependencies.

80
00:02:57,338 --> 00:02:58,874
Could not find artifact.

81
00:02:58,874 --> 00:03:00,090
Commons lang three,

82
00:03:00,090 --> 00:03:00,986
version three,

83
00:03:00,986 --> 00:03:01,562
fourteen,

84
00:03:01,562 --> 00:03:02,330
ninety-nine.

85
00:03:02,330 --> 00:03:04,954
The name of the cause is in the sentence.

86
00:03:05,504 --> 00:03:09,344
Which line of the pom asks for it? Type: grep, dash n, three fourteen, pom dot X M L.

87
00:03:09,894 --> 00:03:13,116
Line sixteen. Version three, fourteen, ninety-nine.

88
00:03:13,666 --> 00:03:14,565
Does that version exist?

89
00:03:14,565 --> 00:03:15,577
Ask the real Maven Central.

90
00:03:15,577 --> 00:03:15,802
First,

91
00:03:15,802 --> 00:03:16,963
keep its address in a variable.

92
00:03:16,963 --> 00:03:17,525
Type: M equals,

93
00:03:17,525 --> 00:03:17,750
https,

94
00:03:17,750 --> 00:03:18,762
repo one dot maven dot org,

95
00:03:18,762 --> 00:03:19,362
slash maven two.

96
00:03:19,912 --> 00:03:24,562
Then the folder of this library, on Central.

97
00:03:25,112 --> 00:03:26,613
Now count how many times Central lists version three,

98
00:03:26,613 --> 00:03:26,867
fourteen,

99
00:03:26,867 --> 00:03:27,207
ninety-nine.

100
00:03:27,207 --> 00:03:27,518
Type: curl,

101
00:03:27,518 --> 00:03:27,717
dash s,

102
00:03:27,717 --> 00:03:28,056
the address,

103
00:03:28,056 --> 00:03:29,075
slash maven dash metadata dot X M L,

104
00:03:29,075 --> 00:03:29,528
and grep dash c.

105
00:03:30,078 --> 00:03:32,830
Zero. Central has never heard of that version.

106
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:36,388
Count version three, fourteen, zero.

107
00:03:38,238 --> 00:03:42,740
One. That one exists. The cause is a wrong version, not a broken network.

108
00:03:43,290 --> 00:03:47,983
Fix the cause. Replace ninety-nine with zero. Type: sed, dash i, and the replacement.

109
00:03:48,533 --> 00:03:51,306
Build again, and keep only the build line.

110
00:03:51,856 --> 00:03:54,672
Now Maven downloads the library from Central.

111
00:04:01,222 --> 00:04:05,852
Build success. One cause, one line fixed, and the dependency is still there.

112
00:04:06,402 --> 00:04:11,266
Failure two. Go into offline. Type: CD, dot dot, slash offline.

113
00:04:11,816 --> 00:04:14,610
Build, and keep only the words about offline mode.

114
00:04:17,860 --> 00:04:20,804
Same dependency, same Central, a different failure.

115
00:04:25,354 --> 00:04:30,154
Cannot access central. Offline mode. Maven is not even trying the network.

116
00:04:30,704 --> 00:04:39,088
Who told Maven to stay offline? Type: cat, dot M V N, slash maven dot config.

117
00:04:39,638 --> 00:04:40,090
Dash O.

118
00:04:40,090 --> 00:04:40,993
A hidden file,

119
00:04:40,993 --> 00:04:41,961
in the project,

120
00:04:41,961 --> 00:04:43,573
adds it to every command.

121
00:04:43,573 --> 00:04:47,766
Offline mode only works when everything is already in your cache.

122
00:04:48,316 --> 00:04:53,330
Remove the file. Type: R M, dot M V N, slash maven dot config.

123
00:04:53,880 --> 00:04:56,653
Build again.

124
00:04:57,203 --> 00:04:58,675
Downloading from Central.

125
00:05:05,225 --> 00:05:06,290
Build success.

126
00:05:06,290 --> 00:05:07,962
A flag is a cause too.

127
00:05:07,962 --> 00:05:11,004
When a build only works on your machine,

128
00:05:11,004 --> 00:05:12,144
look for flags,

129
00:05:12,144 --> 00:05:13,133
in dot M V N,

130
00:05:13,133 --> 00:05:15,870
and in M A V E N underscore A R G S.

131
00:05:16,420 --> 00:05:21,050
Failure three. Go into tests. Type: CD, dot dot, slash tests.

132
00:05:21,600 --> 00:05:26,442
Build, and keep only the line that compares two numbers.

133
00:05:26,992 --> 00:05:29,403
Maven compiles, then runs the tests.

134
00:05:35,953 --> 00:05:37,328
Expected nine hundred,

135
00:05:37,328 --> 00:05:39,327
but was nine hundred and ninety.

136
00:05:39,327 --> 00:05:40,452
The code compiled.

137
00:05:40,452 --> 00:05:43,014
The test is telling us the code is wrong.

138
00:05:43,564 --> 00:05:47,276
Which line computes the discount? Type: grep, dash n, off equals, and the file.

139
00:05:48,426 --> 00:05:49,739
Cents times percent,

140
00:05:49,739 --> 00:05:51,315
divided by one thousand.

141
00:05:51,315 --> 00:05:55,911
A discount of ten percent on one thousand cents should be one hundred.

142
00:05:55,911 --> 00:05:56,896
This gives ten.

143
00:05:57,446 --> 00:06:01,136
Fix the code, not the test. Divide by one hundred.

144
00:06:03,086 --> 00:06:05,838
Build, and keep the test summary and the build line.

145
00:06:08,488 --> 00:06:09,726
The tests run again.

146
00:06:16,276 --> 00:06:16,995
Tests run,

147
00:06:16,995 --> 00:06:17,283
two.

148
00:06:17,283 --> 00:06:17,930
Failures,

149
00:06:17,930 --> 00:06:18,290
zero.

150
00:06:18,290 --> 00:06:19,297
Build success.

151
00:06:19,297 --> 00:06:22,318
Never skip the tests to make this go away.

152
00:06:22,318 --> 00:06:25,556
A test that fails is the build doing its job.

153
00:06:26,106 --> 00:06:31,823
Failure four, the advanced one. Go into login. Type: CD, dot dot, slash login.

154
00:06:32,373 --> 00:06:34,885
This project has its own settings file.

155
00:06:34,885 --> 00:06:37,204
It sends every download to a mirror,

156
00:06:37,204 --> 00:06:38,170
the real Nexus,

157
00:06:38,170 --> 00:06:39,008
with a login.

158
00:06:39,558 --> 00:06:44,144
Build with that settings file, and keep the status code.

159
00:06:45,894 --> 00:06:48,177
Maven asks Nexus for its first file.

160
00:06:53,727 --> 00:06:58,740
Status code four oh one. Unauthorized. The server is there, but it does not know us.

161
00:06:59,290 --> 00:07:01,701
Look at the ids in the settings file. Type: grep, id, settings dot X M L.

162
00:07:02,251 --> 00:07:04,667
The server is called corp dash repo.

163
00:07:04,667 --> 00:07:06,411
The mirror is called corp.

164
00:07:06,411 --> 00:07:07,888
One name is different,

165
00:07:07,888 --> 00:07:09,632
so Maven sent no password.

166
00:07:10,182 --> 00:07:14,321
Fix the id. Make the server match the mirror.

167
00:07:14,871 --> 00:07:18,668
Build again. The password comes from the variable we set at the start.

168
00:07:19,518 --> 00:07:22,420
Now Maven logs in, and downloads through Nexus.

169
00:07:34,970 --> 00:07:39,023
Build success. Same Nexus, same password, one id changed.

170
00:07:39,573 --> 00:07:45,013
Last, the proof. Ask Nexus directly, with no login, and print only the status.

171
00:07:47,163 --> 00:07:50,747
Four oh one. Nexus refuses anyone without a login.

172
00:07:51,297 --> 00:07:54,924
Now ask again, with the user and the password.

173
00:08:00,474 --> 00:08:05,530
Two hundred. Four oh one means: I am here, but who are you. Two hundred means: come in.

174
00:08:07,080 --> 00:08:13,096
Your lab task. Lab ninety-two gives you four broken projects. Lab check judges your fixes.

175
00:08:13,646 --> 00:08:15,800
It lives at git hub dot com,

176
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:17,338
slash it dash waves,

177
00:08:17,338 --> 00:08:19,107
slash dev ops dash A I,

178
00:08:19,107 --> 00:08:19,953
in academy,

179
00:08:19,953 --> 00:08:20,261
lab,

180
00:08:20,261 --> 00:08:22,030
lab ninety-two dot S H.

181
00:08:22,580 --> 00:08:28,041
One: not found. Read which version is missing, and fix the version. Keep the dependency.

182
00:08:28,591 --> 00:08:31,727
Two: offline. Find the hidden flag, and remove it.

183
00:08:32,277 --> 00:08:36,800
Three: tests. Fix the code. Do not skip the tests, and do not edit the test.

184
00:08:37,350 --> 00:08:43,238
Four: login. Make the server id match the mirror id. The password stays in the variable.

185
00:08:43,788 --> 00:08:45,298
Five: in diag dot text,

186
00:08:45,298 --> 00:08:46,414
write four lines,

187
00:08:46,414 --> 00:08:47,464
one per failure,

188
00:08:47,464 --> 00:08:49,761
naming the cause in your own words.

189
00:08:50,311 --> 00:08:52,741
Install a J D K and Maven first.

190
00:08:52,741 --> 00:08:53,652
Then lab up,

191
00:08:53,652 --> 00:08:54,411
lab check,

192
00:08:54,411 --> 00:08:55,398
and lab down.

193
00:08:55,398 --> 00:08:57,903
The first lab up downloads Nexus,

194
00:08:57,903 --> 00:09:00,104
about five hundred megabytes,

195
00:09:00,104 --> 00:09:02,002
so be online and patient.

196
00:09:04,052 --> 00:09:06,121
Pass or fail. You need all six.

197
00:09:06,671 --> 00:09:08,485
Five pass lines in lab check.

198
00:09:09,035 --> 00:09:11,808
You can tell the four failures apart by their message.

199
00:09:12,358 --> 00:09:14,406
You fix the cause, never a symptom.

200
00:09:14,956 --> 00:09:18,455
No dash O, no skip tests, no deleted dependency.

201
00:09:19,005 --> 00:09:21,522
diag dot text names the four causes.

202
00:09:22,072 --> 00:09:23,992
lab down, nothing left behind.

203
00:09:24,542 --> 00:09:25,843
To pass, all six.

204
00:09:27,893 --> 00:09:30,730
Your turn, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine.

205
00:09:31,280 --> 00:09:33,371
One: lab up, and read the task file.

206
00:09:33,921 --> 00:09:37,206
Two: build each project, and read only the first error.

207
00:09:37,756 --> 00:09:39,975
Three: name the cause, in your own words.

208
00:09:40,525 --> 00:09:42,680
Four: fix the cause, and build again.

209
00:09:43,230 --> 00:09:45,939
Five: write diag dot text, and lab check.

210
00:09:46,489 --> 00:09:49,070
Six: lab down, and prove nothing is left.

211
00:09:49,620 --> 00:09:51,455
Pause the video, and begin now.

212
00:10:07,005 --> 00:10:07,880
Quick check.

213
00:10:08,430 --> 00:10:10,968
Which line of a failed build do you read first?

214
00:10:11,518 --> 00:10:13,481
What does four oh four from Central mean?

215
00:10:14,031 --> 00:10:15,908
Why is skip tests never the fix?

216
00:10:16,458 --> 00:10:17,781
What does four oh one mean?

217
00:10:18,331 --> 00:10:21,531
Objective covered: M C ten, objective eight.

218
00:10:22,081 --> 00:10:24,150
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

219
00:10:34,700 --> 00:10:37,751
Next: the maven wrapper, and a build you can repeat.

220
00:10:38,301 --> 00:10:41,629
If this helped, like, share and subscribe, so you do not miss it.
